CD(1)

NAME
     cd - change the working directory

SYNOPSIS
     cd [directory]

DESCRIPTION
     Moves you to another directory. A path that starts with a slash is
     read from the top of the system; any other path is read from where
     you are now. Two dots (..) mean the directory above this one.

     With no directory, takes you back to your home directory.

EXAMPLES
     cd /usr/local/billing
     cd ..
     cd

SEE ALSO
     pwd(1), ls(1)
